+    // BSY Media: a checklist with zero tasks and no status set renders
+    // nothing but this .name div - no .progressRow follows it at all (see
+    // TaskList.jsx's `{(tasks.length > 0 || taskLists.status) && (...)}`
+    // gate). The -2px bottom margin above exists to tighten the gap to that
+    // progressRow when one *is* present; with nothing following, that same
+    // negative margin instead pulls this text flush against (and measured,
+    // slightly past) the card's bottom edge whenever it's the last checklist
+    // on the card. Scoped to :last-child so this only fires in that exact
+    // situation - a checklist followed by a progressRow, more checklists, or
+    // other card content is unaffected.
